-- חוזר לבעלויות תש"פ/10 (24.6.2020): תוכנית היבחנות חדשה בבחינת הבגרות בחטיבה
-- העליונה.
-- How the bagrut reward (גמול בגרות: a percentage and weekly hours) of each
-- subject is divided, under the new examination programme, between the
-- external examination and the school-based assessment.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תש"פ/10 תוכנית היבחנות חדשה בבחינת הבגרות בחטיבה העליונה`

-- The corpus publishes this circular as one undivided heading (hc_1), and
-- its four tables as running paragraphs: each printed row is split over one
-- to three paragraphs, the columns run together, and one fragment survives
-- as a table (hc_1/t1). The rows below are read from those paragraphs; each
-- declaration cites the paragraphs that hold its row.

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of upper-secondary institutions), greeting and subject; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p14 The statement that the circular consolidates circulars תשע"ה/2, תשע"ט/9 and תש"פ/2; a source note, no rule of its own.
-- akn:hc_1/p15 The statement that the circular holds a table dividing the bagrut reward between the external examination and the school-based assessment; the table is encoded below.
-- akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p17 akn:hc_1/p18 akn:hc_1/p19 The sign-off and signature, printed before the tables; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21 akn:hc_1/p22 akn:hc_1/p23 akn:hc_1/p24 akn:hc_1/p25 akn:hc_1/p26 akn:hc_1/p27 akn:hc_1/p28 akn:hc_1/p29 akn:hc_1/p30 akn:hc_1/p31 The copies list; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p32 akn:hc_1/p33 akn:hc_1/p34 akn:hc_1/p35 akn:hc_1/p36 akn:hc_1/p37 akn:hc_1/p38 akn:hc_1/p39 akn:hc_1/p40 akn:hc_1/p41 akn:hc_1/p42 The copies list, continued; no rule.

@desc One printed row: a subject's examination component and its bagrut reward before the reform and, under it, split between the external examination and the school-based assessment. Percentages as fractions (2% is 0.02); a blank cell is 0.
DECLARE `reward row` HAS
    `subject`               IS A STRING
    `units`                 IS A NUMBER
    `component`             IS A STRING  @desc the questionnaire or task, as printed (old number / new number)
    `pre-reform hours`      IS A NUMBER
    `pre-reform percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `external hours`        IS A NUMBER
    `external percentage`   IS A NUMBER
    `school hours`          IS A NUMBER
    `school percentage`     IS A NUMBER

-- The tables' column headings: subject, units, pre-reform reward (in weekly
-- hours and in percent), reform reward — external (70%) and school-based
-- (30%), each in weekly hours and in percent — and remarks.
-- akn:hc_1/p44 akn:hc_1/p45 akn:hc_1/p46 akn:hc_1/p47 akn:hc_1/p48 The first table's column headings; encoded as the fields of `reward row`.
-- akn:hc_1/p65 akn:hc_1/p66 akn:hc_1/p67 akn:hc_1/p68 akn:hc_1/p69 akn:hc_1/p70 akn:hc_1/p71 akn:hc_1/p72 The second table's column headings; encoded as the fields of `reward row`.
-- akn:hc_1/p89 akn:hc_1/p90 akn:hc_1/p91 akn:hc_1/p92 akn:hc_1/p93 The third table's column headings; encoded as the fields of `reward row`.
-- akn:hc_1/p112 akn:hc_1/p113 akn:hc_1/p114 akn:hc_1/p115 akn:hc_1/p116 The fourth table's column headings; encoded as the fields of `reward row`.
-- akn:hc_1/p135 akn:hc_1/p136 akn:hc_1/p137 akn:hc_1/p138 akn:hc_1/p139 The fifth table's column headings; encoded as the fields of `reward row`.

§§ `Compulsory subjects: mathematics`

-- p49's remark: the school-based bagrut in 3-unit mathematics is questionnaire
-- 35183. p143's note: in 4- and 5-unit mathematics nothing changes from
-- before the reform; the bagrut is external only.
@ref akn:hc_1/p43 akn:hc_1/p49 akn:hc_1/p50 akn:hc_1/p51 akn:hc_1/p52 akn:hc_1/p53 akn:hc_1/p54 akn:hc_1/p55 akn:hc_1/p56 akn:hc_1/p57 akn:hc_1/p58 akn:hc_1/p59 akn:hc_1/p60 akn:hc_1/p61 akn:hc_1/p62 akn:hc_1/p63 akn:hc_1/p64 akn:hc_1/p143
`the mathematics rows` MEANS
    LIST `reward row` "mathematics" 3 "801 / 035183"     0.5  0.02 0    0    0.5 0.02,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 3 "802 / 035381"     0.5  0.02 0.5  0.02 0   0,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 3 "803 / 035382"     1    0.02 1    0.02 0   0,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 4 "804+803 / 035481" 2    0.04 2    0.04 0   0,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 4 "805 / 035482"     1    0.02 1    0.02 0   0,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 5 "806+805 / 035581" 2.25 0.04 2.25 0.04 0   0,
         `reward row` "mathematics" 5 "807 / 035582"     1.25 0.02 1.25 0.02 0   0

