         `reward row` "English"      5 "E / 016481" 1    0.02 1    0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "English"      5 "F / 016583" 1.25 0.02 0    0     1.25 0.02,
         `reward row` "English"      5 "G / 016582" 1.25 0.02 1.25 0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "Bible (state)" 2 "examination" 1.5 0.02 1.05 0.014 0.45 0.006

§§ `Compulsory subjects: the rest`

-- p95's remark: Bible (religious) has two external questionnaires and the
-- external reward is divided between them equally. p101–102: civics' 0.4
-- weekly hours are the performance task's reward as before the reform.
-- p106–108: for teachers entering pupils in the 50% external / 50%
-- school-based project, Hebrew language and expression divides 1 hour + 2%
-- to each.
@ref akn:hc_1/p94 akn:hc_1/p95 akn:hc_1/p96 akn:hc_1/p97 akn:hc_1/p98 akn:hc_1/p99 akn:hc_1/p100 akn:hc_1/p101 akn:hc_1/p102 akn:hc_1/p103 akn:hc_1/p104 akn:hc_1/p105 akn:hc_1/p106 akn:hc_1/p109 akn:hc_1/p110
`the other compulsory rows` MEANS
    LIST `reward row` "Bible (religious)"                      3 "examination"      2   0.02 1.4  0.014 0.6  0.006,
         `reward row` "Oral Torah (religious)"                 3 "examination"      2   0.02 1.4  0.014 0.6  0.006,
         `reward row` "Judaism (Haredi)"                       3 "examination"      2   0.02 1.4  0.014 0.6  0.006,
         `reward row` "Druze heritage / Islam / Christianity"  1 "examination"      1   0.02 0.7  0.014 0.3  0.006,
         `reward row` "history"                                2 "examination"      1.5 0.02 1.05 0.014 0.45 0.006,
         `reward row` "civics"                                 2 "questionnaire"    1.5 0.02 1.5  0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "civics"                                 2 "performance task" 0.4 0    0    0     0.4  0,
         `reward row` "literature"                             2 "examination"      1.5 0.02 1.05 0.014 0.45 0.006,
         `reward row` "literature (religious)"                 1 "examination"      1   0.02 0.7  0.014 0.3  0.006,
         `reward row` "Jewish thought (religious)"             1 "examination"      1   0.02 0.7  0.014 0.3  0.006,
         `reward row` "Hebrew language and expression"         2 "examination"      2   0.04 1.4  0.028 0.6  0.012,
         `reward row` "Arabic language and literature"         3 "examination"      2   0.02 1.4  0.014 0.6  0.006,
         `reward row` "Hebrew language and literature (non-Jewish sector)" 3 "examination" 2 0.02 1.4 0.014 0.6 0.006

-- p95: the two external questionnaires of Bible (religious) share the
-- external reward equally.
@ref akn:hc_1/p95
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `each external questionnaire's hours in religious Bible` r IS
    r's `external hours` DIVIDED BY 2

-- p107–108: the project's 50/50 division of Hebrew language and expression.
@ref akn:hc_1/p107 akn:hc_1/p108
`the Hebrew-expression project row` MEANS
    `reward row` "Hebrew language and expression (project)" 2 "examination" 2 0.04 1 0.02 1 0.02

§§ `Electives with special instructions`

-- The asterisked remarks: the school-based reward of the biotope /
-- bio-research, ecotope and geotope is the one paid before the reform.
-- p126–127: geography's external weight is 60% and school-based 40%;
-- p130–131: Land of Israel studies' external weight is 30% and school-based 70%.
@ref akn:hc_1/p111 akn:hc_1/p117 akn:hc_1/p118 akn:hc_1/p119 akn:hc_1/p120 akn:hc_1/p121 akn:hc_1/p122 akn:hc_1/p123 akn:hc_1/p124 akn:hc_1/p125 akn:hc_1/p126 akn:hc_1/p127 akn:hc_1/p128 akn:hc_1/p129 akn:hc_1/p130 akn:hc_1/p131 akn:hc_1/p132 akn:hc_1/p133
`the special elective rows` MEANS
    LIST `reward row` "biology"                         5 "questionnaire and laboratory" 3.5 0.02 3.5  0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "biology"                         5 "biotope / bio-research"       1.5 0    0    0     1.5  0,
         `reward row` "life sciences and agriculture"   5 "questionnaire"                3.5 0.02 3.5  0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "life sciences and agriculture"   5 "biotope / bio-research"       1.5 0    0    0     1.5  0,
         `reward row` "environmental sciences"          5 "questionnaire"                3.5 0.02 3.5  0.02  0    0,
         `reward row` "environmental sciences"          5 "ecotope"                      1.5 0    0    0     1.5  0,
         `reward row` "geography"                       5 "questionnaire"                3.5 0.02 2.1  0.012 1.4  0.008,
         `reward row` "geography"                       5 "geotope"                      1   0    0    0     1    0,
         `reward row` "Land of Israel studies"          5 "questionnaire"                3.5 0.02 1.05 0.006 2.45 0.014,
         `reward row` "Land of Israel studies"          5 "geotope"                      1   0    0    0     1    0

§§ `All other electives`

-- p141–142: in Bible (state-religious) the external weight is 50% and the
-- school-based 50%; each divides between two questionnaires or examination
-- events — the external equally (25% each), the school-based into 20% and
-- 30%.
@ref akn:hc_1/p134 akn:hc_1/p140 akn:hc_1/p141 akn:hc_1/p142
`the other elective rows` MEANS
    LIST `reward row` "any other elective subject" 5 "examination" 3.5 0.02 2.45 0.014 1.05 0.006,
         `reward row` "Bible (state-religious)"    5 "examination" 3.5 0.02 1.75 0.01  1.75 0.01

`all the rows` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the mathematics rows`, `the English and state Bible rows`, `the other compulsory rows`,
                 `the special elective rows`, `the other elective rows`)

-- p144: where a field divides its examination otherwise than 70% / 30%, the
-- reward divides in the same proportion — "for example Chinese, German, the
-- Arab world and Islam, social sciences". The proportion is the field's own,
-- an input; F-2019-20_tashaf_10-a.
@ref akn:hc_1/p144
@desc The external examination's share of a field's bagrut where it is not 70%; set by the field, not printed in this circular.
ASSUME `the field's external share` IS A FUNCTION FROM STRING TO NUMBER

`the fields p144 names as dividing otherwise` MEANS
    LIST "Chinese", "German", "the Arab world and Islam", "social sciences"

-- The share of the reform reward that goes to the external examination, by
-- the printed rows: "any other elective subject" is 70%.
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the external share the table prints for an elective` s IS
    IF elem s (LIST "geography", "Land of Israel studies", "Bible (state-religious)")
    THEN CONSIDER s
         WHEN "geography" THEN 0.6
         WHEN "Land of Israel studies" THEN 0.3
         OTHERWISE 0.5
    ELSE 0.7

`a field p144 names as dividing otherwise falls in the table's 70% row` MEANS
        elem "German" `the fields p144 names as dividing otherwise`
    AND `the external share the table prints for an elective` "German" EQUALS 0.7
#ASSERT `a field p144 names as dividing otherwise falls in the table's 70% row`

-- p142: the school-based half of Bible (state-religious) divides 20% / 30%
-- between its two events, and the circular does not say which takes which;
-- F-2019-20_tashaf_10-b. Both assignments, for the first event's hours:
GIVEN `the first event takes the larger part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the first school-based event's hours in state-religious Bible` `the first event takes the larger part` IS
    IF `the first event takes the larger part`
    THEN 3.5 TIMES 0.3
    ELSE 3.5 TIMES 0.2

`the two school-based events of state-religious Bible can be paid either way` MEANS
    NOT (`the first school-based event's hours in state-religious Bible` TRUE
         EQUALS `the first school-based event's hours in state-religious Bible` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the two school-based events of state-religious Bible can be paid either way`

-- The reward for a component under the reform, for a teacher preparing a
-- class for the external examination, the school-based assessment, or both.
@export The bagrut reward of one examination component under the new examination programme, split between external and school-based parts, per circular תש"פ/10
GIVEN r IS A `reward row` @desc the printed row of the subject's component
      `prepares the external examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `conducts the school-based assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A PAIR OF NUMBER, NUMBER
DECIDE `the reform reward` r `prepares the external examination` `conducts the school-based assessment` IS
    PAIR OF `hours`, `percentage`
    WHERE
        `external part` MEANS IF `prepares the external examination` THEN 1 ELSE 0
        `school part`   MEANS IF `conducts the school-based assessment` THEN 1 ELSE 0
        `hours`         MEANS `external part` TIMES r's `external hours` PLUS `school part` TIMES r's `school hours`
        `percentage`    MEANS `external part` TIMES r's `external percentage` PLUS `school part` TIMES r's `school percentage`

-- Examples.
-- Every printed row conserves the pre-reform reward: external plus
-- school-based equals what was paid before, in hours and in percent.
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row conserves the reward` r IF
        r's `external hours` PLUS r's `school hours` EQUALS r's `pre-reform hours`
    AND r's `external percentage` PLUS r's `school percentage` EQUALS r's `pre-reform percentage`

#ASSERT all `the row conserves the reward` `all the rows`
#ASSERT `the row conserves the reward` `the Hebrew-expression project row`

-- The rows the remarks do not single out split 70 / 30.
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`, share IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row splits` r share IF
        r's `external hours` EQUALS r's `pre-reform hours` TIMES share
    AND r's `external percentage` EQUALS r's `pre-reform percentage` TIMES share

#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD `the row splits` r 0.7)
            (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `external hours` GREATER THAN 0 AND r's `school hours` GREATER THAN 0
                                   AND (NOT elem (r's `subject`) (LIST "geography", "Land of Israel studies", "Bible (state-religious)")))
                    `all the rows`)
#ASSERT `the row splits` (`reward row` "geography" 5 "questionnaire" 3.5 0.02 2.1 0.012 1.4 0.008) 0.6
#ASSERT `the row splits` (`reward row` "Land of Israel studies" 5 "questionnaire" 3.5 0.02 1.05 0.006 2.45 0.014) 0.3
#ASSERT `the row splits` (`reward row` "Bible (state-religious)" 5 "examination" 3.5 0.02 1.75 0.01 1.75 0.01) 0.5

`the history row` MEANS `reward row` "history" 2 "examination" 1.5 0.02 1.05 0.014 0.45 0.006
#ASSERT `the reform reward` `the history row` TRUE TRUE EQUALS PAIR OF 1.5, 0.02
#ASSERT `the reform reward` `the history row` TRUE FALSE EQUALS PAIR OF 1.05, 0.014
#EVAL count `all the rows`
